    "media:imagetext": "•The supersonic jet Concorde in Braniff International markings flies\nbetween Dallas-Fort Worth and London and Paris in cooperation\nwith British Airways and Air France. Braniff flight crews fly the\nConcorde at the subsonic speed of Mach 0.95 between Dallas-\nFort Worth and Washington, D.C. Flight time between the two cities is\n20% taster. This is the only domestic Concorde service. Between\nWashington and London or Paris, British and French air crews fly at\nthe supersonic speed of Mach 2.0 (1,350 miles per hour). Braniff is\nthe first U.S. airline to fly the Concorde.\n2015.166.2570",
